   "rule": "The root's sway and squash move the ViewportFrame on the screen, not the camera: its AnchorPoint on `origin`, placed at origin + at.x per_x + at.z per_z, sized the screen times (scale.x, scale.z). The leak's cells ride with it, sized by the same."
  },
  "seams": {
   "cracks": "each rarity's `cracks`, seams A to D",
   "gap": "0.045 snap(t - crack) widen(t)",
   "widen": "the most over the steps passed of 1 + (wide - 1) smooth((t - when) / 0.08); 1 before any"
  },
  "pose": {
   "shake": "0 before 0; 0.006 + 0.022 level widen / 2",
   "at": "(sin(173 t) shake, 0.03 sin(3.1 t) + sin(211 t + 1) shake)",
   "tap": "exp(-t / 0.035) from 0: scale (1 + 0.07 tap, 1 - 0.07 tap)",
   "rise": "with a climb: 0.25 smooth((t - 0.4) / 0.6) added to at.z",
   "swell": "1 + 0.05 smooth((t - (split - 0.15)) / 0.15); with a breath (b0, b1): 1 + 0.06 smooth((t - 0.4) / 0.6) - 0.16 smooth((t - b0) / (b1 - b0) 1.4), and from b0 at is (0.2 at.x, 0.2 at.z + 0.03) before the rise; scale times swell",
   "rung": "each step after the first, i from 0, age = t - when, amp = 0.6 + 0.4 lv, while 0 <= age < 0.3: scale times 1 + 0.05 amp bump(age); jolt = 0.08 amp exp(-age / 0.025) cos(age / 0.05 2 pi); at.x plus jolt (minus for odd i), at.z plus 0.35 jolt",
   "fly": "reach (1 - exp(-tau / 0.13)) from the split",
   "spin": "max(0, tau) 5 + fly 0.22",
   "core": "1 to the split, then max(0, 1 - tau / 0.09): the core's scale",
   "piece": "location = side_A A_normal gap_A / 2 + (its seam's way along gap) + away fly reach; rotation (Blender's XYZ, written for Roblox) = Y((2 - i) spin 0.3) * Z(-(i - 2) spin 0.8) * X((0.5 + i) spin 0.6), each CFrame.fromAxisAngle, i the piece's order",
   "A_normal": [
    -0.53613,
    0.82535,
    -0.17707
   ],
   "fade": "the pieces' cover 1 - smooth((tau - 0.18) / 0.25)"
  },
  "core_colour": "mix(#07050C, mix(light, white, 0.55 + 0.45 level), min(1, level + 0.35))",
  "leak": "Every cell is in reveal_leak, anchored on the root, sized the root's scale. m = min(1, level + 0.35), k = the core's scale, burn the rung's push. The cells come in nine sets, i = 0 to 8 (sets): 0 to 2 the seams cracked one by one (A, AB, ABC) at their width, 3 to 8 all four at each rung's width (1, 1.2, 1.45, 1.7, 2.3, 2.8). Which show: snap_n = snap(t - crack n) for each crack; n = the cracks begun. None before the first. While n < 4 or snap_4 < 1: f = min(1, snap_n); set n-2 by 1 - f and set n-1 by blend(f) (n = 1: set 0 by f alone); over = max(1, mean of snap_1..n) times widen (the rungs' widening, the pose's rule). After: widen picks the two rung sets either side of it, f by how near it is to the upper (past 2.8, set 8 alone): the lower by 1 - f, the upper by blend(f); over = max(1, mean of the four snaps). blend(f) = f / (1 - 0.6 (1 - f)). Lay the lower set first. burn' = burn over. a = m level burn' k; b = a once the first rung has come, else no beams; c = m burn' k. piecesHot and hot cells are white, the rest tinted the light. A cell's alpha at its drive x: with a scale, min(1, x / scale); with a ramp [lo, hi], clamp((x - lo) / (hi - lo), 0, 1); with a curve ([x, alpha] points), straight between them, held past the ends. For each kind in this order, each picked set's cell and then its Boost, alpha times the set's share: wide<i> from a; piecesHot<i> from a; beams<i> from b; tight<i> from c; hot<i> from c. A cell missing from the atlas had nothing in it: skip it."
 },
